[{:db/id 17592186179744 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-90df2f56-7b61-5a49-aa6d-4d0c58b35b14" "question-b2007897-e589-5e81-a8ff-d3a65c150dee"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179745 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3e7323f9-19dc-5d6f-a8c7-1664ab5ee0f5"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179746 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-735394db-bfa6-5cb2-9d7d-19fe3d01e994" "question-ddff35a9-8792-529b-9827-d26481dbe529"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-90df2f56-7b61-5a49-aa6d-4d0c58b35b14" :question/id #uuid "90df2f56-7b61-5a49-aa6d-4d0c58b35b14" :question/math-academy-id "q-127062" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+{e}^{x}\\,j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & ={e}^{y}={e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}, \\\\ Q(x,y) & ={e}^{x}={e}^{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral using the substitutions $u=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,du=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt$ and $v=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,dv=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\cdot (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-({e}^{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\cdot (4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0}{e}^{u}\\,du-{\\int }_{1}^{1}{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-452bd17e-660a-568a-8108-39d6d0770162"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-452bd17e-660a-568a-8108-39d6d0770162" :answer-field/id #uuid "452bd17e-660a-568a-8108-39d6d0770162" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-093b5f1d-7084-5cca-af48-56a7c276ea5d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1755e313-29bb-5235-930c-5480eea8e580" "answer-2a42ddb5-8533-50f3-9230-498c83bae1a9" "answer-093b5f1d-7084-5cca-af48-56a7c276ea5d" "answer-c7b8c70b-0bf4-5466-85d5-56e8bfa6fc37" "answer-93070110-72d1-593c-aaa7-f43291b04560"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1755e313-29bb-5235-930c-5480eea8e580" :answer/id #uuid "1755e313-29bb-5235-930c-5480eea8e580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{25e}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a42ddb5-8533-50f3-9230-498c83bae1a9" :answer/id #uuid "2a42ddb5-8533-50f3-9230-498c83bae1a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{7e}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-093b5f1d-7084-5cca-af48-56a7c276ea5d" :answer/id #uuid "093b5f1d-7084-5cca-af48-56a7c276ea5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7b8c70b-0bf4-5466-85d5-56e8bfa6fc37" :answer/id #uuid "c7b8c70b-0bf4-5466-85d5-56e8bfa6fc37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{25e}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-93070110-72d1-593c-aaa7-f43291b04560" :answer/id #uuid "93070110-72d1-593c-aaa7-f43291b04560" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7e}{12}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-b2007897-e589-5e81-a8ff-d3a65c150dee" :question/id #uuid "b2007897-e589-5e81-a8ff-d3a65c150dee" :question/math-academy-id "q-127082" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)=x\\,i+(x+y)\\,j$ across the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & =x=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =x+y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral using the substitution $\\operatorname{sin}⁡t=u,du=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }15{cos}^{2}⁡t+9\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+15{sin}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }15\\,\\text{d}t+9{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }15\\,\\text{d}t+9{\\int }_{0}^{0}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =15t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi }+0 \\\\  & =15(2\\pi -0) \\\\  & =30\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-8411ac91-aa07-508a-9904-aa0a020877bc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-8411ac91-aa07-508a-9904-aa0a020877bc" :answer-field/id #uuid "8411ac91-aa07-508a-9904-aa0a020877bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3cf1e009-304c-5363-9a50-24170560d53d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-29d3016e-ea1f-57be-ad3f-89bd52e2b595" "answer-29d80bea-8d5f-5d6e-9d57-a11322c402b1" "answer-eb22ea92-b3d9-59e8-9fe5-49b32e301c4f" "answer-2cd76549-ed5c-561a-a07f-a7506fbab6d4" "answer-3cf1e009-304c-5363-9a50-24170560d53d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29d3016e-ea1f-57be-ad3f-89bd52e2b595" :answer/id #uuid "29d3016e-ea1f-57be-ad3f-89bd52e2b595" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29d80bea-8d5f-5d6e-9d57-a11322c402b1" :answer/id #uuid "29d80bea-8d5f-5d6e-9d57-a11322c402b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-30\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb22ea92-b3d9-59e8-9fe5-49b32e301c4f" :answer/id #uuid "eb22ea92-b3d9-59e8-9fe5-49b32e301c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2cd76549-ed5c-561a-a07f-a7506fbab6d4" :answer/id #uuid "2cd76549-ed5c-561a-a07f-a7506fbab6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cf1e009-304c-5363-9a50-24170560d53d" :answer/id #uuid "3cf1e009-304c-5363-9a50-24170560d53d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-3e7323f9-19dc-5d6f-a8c7-1664ab5ee0f5" :question/id #uuid "3e7323f9-19dc-5d6f-a8c7-1664ab5ee0f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-127147" :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)={e}^{y}\\,i+{e}^{x}\\,j$ across the ellipse $C$ with equation $4{x}^{2}+25{y}^{2}=100.$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nFirst, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $5$ and $2,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & ={e}^{y}={e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t}, \\\\ Q(x,y) & ={e}^{x}={e}^{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral using the substitutions $u=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,du=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,dt$ and $v=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,dv=-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,dt,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-({e}^{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t})\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({e}^{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t})\\cdot (-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{0}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u+{\\int }_{1}^{1}{e}^{v}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b62610d8-6a5e-55a5-8cf3-f983d7201b32"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b62610d8-6a5e-55a5-8cf3-f983d7201b32" :answer-field/id #uuid "b62610d8-6a5e-55a5-8cf3-f983d7201b32" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cb802d80-52ae-51ef-9629-c1c85410bffa" :answer-field/choices ["answer-37855248-eec6-54d6-abfc-d67f62c8a619" "answer-cb802d80-52ae-51ef-9629-c1c85410bffa" "answer-77c54161-201d-5420-8d49-397874bb229d" "answer-9a40d272-dad6-5203-a06f-4c1b6242a085" "answer-fbbebcc7-a768-5300-b557-75982c0cd1f5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-37855248-eec6-54d6-abfc-d67f62c8a619" :answer/id #uuid "37855248-eec6-54d6-abfc-d67f62c8a619" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cb802d80-52ae-51ef-9629-c1c85410bffa" :answer/id #uuid "cb802d80-52ae-51ef-9629-c1c85410bffa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77c54161-201d-5420-8d49-397874bb229d" :answer/id #uuid "77c54161-201d-5420-8d49-397874bb229d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2}(1-{e}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9a40d272-dad6-5203-a06f-4c1b6242a085" :answer/id #uuid "9a40d272-dad6-5203-a06f-4c1b6242a085" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{2}(1-{e}^{3})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fbbebcc7-a768-5300-b557-75982c0cd1f5" :answer/id #uuid "fbbebcc7-a768-5300-b557-75982c0cd1f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180041 :question/problem "Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\,i+xy\\,j$ across the ellipse $C$ with equation $4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=36.$" :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple, closed curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ denotes the outward-pointing unit normal vector to $C.$ \n\nFirst, we write the equation of our curve as\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nThe closed curve $C$ is an ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal and vertical semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ respectively. It can be parameterized in the counterclockwise direction as\n\n$$\nr(t)=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j,\\,0\\le t\\le 2\\pi .\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & ={y}^{2}=4{sin}^{2}⁡t, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =xy=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(4{sin}^{2}⁡t)\\cdot (2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)-(6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }8{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+18{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }26{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{1}26{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177915 :answer-field/correct 17592186177919 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-735394db-bfa6-5cb2-9d7d-19fe3d01e994" :question/id #uuid "735394db-bfa6-5cb2-9d7d-19fe3d01e994" :question/math-academy-id "q-127256" :question/problem "![](images/62/62c8f6d7db345ce76bd164bb52c13e5edef9c04f18f4f07501c8694e7f64b554.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ is given by $x={e}^{y}$ from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(e,1).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)={y}^{2}\\,i+\\frac{1}{x}\\,j$ through $C,$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector $n$ on $C,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ measured with respect to a unit normal vector $n$ on $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply this formula, \n\n- the curve should be parameterized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector $n$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nParameterizing the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={e}^{t}\\,y=t,\\,t\\in [0,1].\n$$\n\n \n\nThis parameterization traverses the curve from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(e,1).$ Therefore, $n$ is indeed a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of $T,$ so we can apply the above formula for the flux. \n\n![](images/ba/ba6285008fd90835fdbf73203b76a0a01d713889d9939979aaec54bebd0a8c49.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & ={y}^{2}={t}^{2}, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =\\frac{1}{x}={e}^{-t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2})\\cdot (1)-({e}^{-t})\\cdot ({e}^{t})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}-1\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-t){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-1)-0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-04fdbb04-1f5e-524e-9c27-6e5e40173080"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-04fdbb04-1f5e-524e-9c27-6e5e40173080" :answer-field/id #uuid "04fdbb04-1f5e-524e-9c27-6e5e40173080" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6097d82c-a160-580e-ba98-359ee8f02940" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5f942441-ff7e-546f-8b6c-c0bc3ed8b008" "answer-6097d82c-a160-580e-ba98-359ee8f02940" "answer-8ebff72e-dab2-5efc-93c1-8a98f5c588a0" "answer-a5ebd4b0-5c2f-5c66-823d-14cb8a9a334c" "answer-54352619-e7d8-51ab-bf81-2466d57fb916"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f942441-ff7e-546f-8b6c-c0bc3ed8b008" :answer/id #uuid "5f942441-ff7e-546f-8b6c-c0bc3ed8b008" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6097d82c-a160-580e-ba98-359ee8f02940" :answer/id #uuid "6097d82c-a160-580e-ba98-359ee8f02940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ebff72e-dab2-5efc-93c1-8a98f5c588a0" :answer/id #uuid "8ebff72e-dab2-5efc-93c1-8a98f5c588a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a5ebd4b0-5c2f-5c66-823d-14cb8a9a334c" :answer/id #uuid "a5ebd4b0-5c2f-5c66-823d-14cb8a9a334c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-54352619-e7d8-51ab-bf81-2466d57fb916" :answer/id #uuid "54352619-e7d8-51ab-bf81-2466d57fb916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ddff35a9-8792-529b-9827-d26481dbe529" :question/id #uuid "ddff35a9-8792-529b-9827-d26481dbe529" :question/math-academy-id "q-127235" :question/problem "![](images/95/95e6a455863f0b4cefe184cca9ad86feaeff9f0702808db2d151f5d6615a04b8.png)\n\nThe curve $C$ is given by $y=\\frac{1}{x}$ from the point $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$ to the point $(2,\\frac{1}{2}).$ Calculate the flux of the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{2}y\\,i-y\\,j$ through $C,$ measured with respect to the unit normal vector $n$ on $C,$ as shown above." :question/worked-solution "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field and $C$ is a piecewise-smooth, simple curve, then the flux of $F$ across $C$ measured with respect to a unit normal vector $n$ on $C$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo apply this formula, \n\n- the curve should be parameterized as $r(t)$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ and\n\n- the unit normal vector $n$ *must* be a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of the unit tangent vector $T(t).$\n\nParameterizing the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t,\\,y=\\frac{1}{t},\\,t\\in [\\frac{1}{2},2].\n$$\n\n \n\nThis parameterization traverses the curve from the point $(\\frac{1}{2},2)$ to the point $(2,\\frac{1}{2}).$ Therefore, $n$ is indeed a ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise rotation of $T,$ so we can apply the above formula for the flux. \n\n![](images/cc/cc9d66f800a57f27673577cd3fd179b4cd6ff64585c5dc1a867317d8d592e485.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x,y) & ={x}^{2}y=t, \\\\ Q(x,y) & =-y=-\\frac{1}{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the derivatives of $x(t)$ and $y(t)$ along the curve, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})=-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}(P\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}-Q\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t})\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}(t)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}})-(-\\frac{1}{t})\\cdot (1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1/2}^{2}0\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-5f7eefb0-93b0-549d-9805-f25d2ffc89e0"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-5f7eefb0-93b0-549d-9805-f25d2ffc89e0" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f7eefb0-93b0-549d-9805-f25d2ffc89e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0a0fbaf0-fbaf-5ffb-ba78-e300b9c3cb2c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-527da9e8-31b2-5d12-ada1-f6448689e756" "answer-d6be670d-4038-5dbc-ac98-7208e5a8c53f" "answer-0a0fbaf0-fbaf-5ffb-ba78-e300b9c3cb2c" "answer-b79b1436-2e95-5a91-a8c3-0d137af242fb" "answer-dfbe47bf-91a3-5026-b0f2-e265e56e1b7f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-527da9e8-31b2-5d12-ada1-f6448689e756" :answer/id #uuid "527da9e8-31b2-5d12-ada1-f6448689e756" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d6be670d-4038-5dbc-ac98-7208e5a8c53f" :answer/id #uuid "d6be670d-4038-5dbc-ac98-7208e5a8c53f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a0fbaf0-fbaf-5ffb-ba78-e300b9c3cb2c" :answer/id #uuid "0a0fbaf0-fbaf-5ffb-ba78-e300b9c3cb2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b79b1436-2e95-5a91-a8c3-0d137af242fb" :answer/id #uuid "b79b1436-2e95-5a91-a8c3-0d137af242fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfbe47bf-91a3-5026-b0f2-e265e56e1b7f" :answer/id #uuid "dfbe47bf-91a3-5026-b0f2-e265e56e1b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180728 :tutorial/content "Let's now derive the following formula for the flux:\n\n$$\n\\oint\\limits_C \\mathbf F \\cdot \\mathbf{n} \\: \\textrm{d}s = \\oint\\limits_C P\\,\\textrm{d}y- Q\\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nFirst, recall that if $C$ is parameterized by the function $\\mathbf r(t) = x(t)\\,\\mathbf i + y(t)\\,\\mathbf j$ for $t\\in [a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\mathbf n = \\dfrac{y'(t)\\,\\mathbf i - x'(t)\\,\\mathbf j}{||\\mathbf r'(t)||},\n$$\n\nwhere it is assumed that $C$ is positively-oriented. \n\nSubstituting our expression for $\\mathbf n$ into our line integral definition of flux and using the fact that $\\textrm d s = ||\\mathbf r'(t)|| \\,\\textrm d t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s & ={∮}_{C}(P(x(t),y(t))\\,i+Q(x(t),y(t))\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)\\,i-{x}^{′}(t)\\,j}{||{r}^{′}(t)||})||{r}^{′}(t)||\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}(P(x(t),y(t))\\,i+Q(x(t),y(t))\\,j)\\cdot (\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)\\,i-{x}^{′}(t)\\,j}{\\cancel{||{r}^{′}(t)||}})\\cancel{||{r}^{′}(t)||}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}(P(x(t),y(t))\\,i+Q(x(t),y(t))\\,j)\\cdot ({y}^{′}(t)\\,i-{x}^{′}(t)\\,j)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P(x(t),y(t)){y}^{′}(t)-Q(x(t),y(t)){x}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={∮}_{C}P\\,\\text{d}y-Q\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179867 :activity/expected-seconds 1200.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
